  "text": "\r\n         Town of Milford, NH -  \r\n     Skip to main content \r\nDepartments \nMain Menu  /  Departments \nDepartments \nAll Departments \nADA Compliance \nAmbulance \nAssessing \nBuilding Safety \nCommunity Development \nCommunity Media \nFinance \nFire Department \nHealth Department \nHuman Resources \nInformation Technology \nLibrary \nEmergency Management \nPlanning and GIS \nPolice Department \nPublic Works \nRecreation \nRecycling & Transfer Station \nStormwater Management \nTax Collection \nTown Administrator \nTown Clerk \nWater Utilities \nWelfare Department \nBoards \nMain Menu  /  Boards \nBoards \nAll Boards \nArtWalk Committee \nBudget Advisory Committee \nCemetery Trustees \nCIP Citizens Advisory Committee \nConservation Commission \nEconomic Development Advisory Council \nEnergy Advisory Committee \nEthics Committee \nGranite Town Media Advisory Committee \nHeritage Commission \nJoint Loss Management Committee \nLibrary Trustees \nMACC Base \nMaster Plan Steering Committee \nPlanning Board \nRecreation Commission \nRecycling Committee \nSelect Board \nTraffic Safety Committee \nTrustees of the Trust Fund \nVietnam Memorial Committee \nWater and Sewer Commissioners \nZoning Board of Adjustement \n250th Celebration Committee \nTown Government \nMain Menu  /  Town Government \nTown Government \nAbout Milford \nDepartments \nBoards \nElected Officials \nEmployment \nMinutes & Agendas \nActive Projects \nMunicipal Codes \nMaps / GIS Mapping \nContact Us \nResidents \nMain Menu  /  Residents \nResidents \nPermits, Forms & Links \nDepartment Directory \nUtility & Service Providers \nCommunity Power \nE Services & Payments \nVolunteer Opportunities \nSchools \nLibrary \nCemeteries \nNews & Public Notices \nCommunity Calendar \nBusiness \nMain Menu  /  Business \nBusiness \nLocal Business Organizations \nStarting a Business \nState & Regional Resources                                  \r\n                             Quick Links \r\n                             About Milford \r\n                             News & Public Notices \r\n                             Town Reports \r\n                             Calendar \r\nWelcome to the Town of Milford, NH! \r\n                             Welcome to the Town of Milford, NH! \r\nQuick Links \n2026 Election/Budget Info \nAgendas & Minutes \nForms & Documents \nE Services & Payments \nMeeting Videos & Podcasts \nOval/ Transfer Station/ Keyes Cameras \nOpen RFPs \nMilford Alerts \nAbout Milford \nAbout Milford, NH \nThe Town of Milford has a rich history.  Separated from Amherst and established as an independent town in 1794, Milford was a prime stop on the Underground Railroad. Located in southern New Hampshire on the banks of the Souhegan River, the town is named after the River's shallow Mill Ford, so called after the many mills at this location in the eighteenth century. Milford is still a favorable spot for business.  \nMade famous by the thriving granite industry and known as The Granite Town in the Granite State, Milford is home to manufacturing, information and service oriented businesses. The town is also a hotspot for tourism and is especially known for its antique shops and country craft stores. \nWhether you live, work, shop or do business here, Milford NH has something for you. Our historic downtown is in the heart of the community... Take a leisurely stroll and you'll realize why Milford is \" The Granite Town in the Granite State .\" We're proud to serve as the hub of the region for living, business, and shopping. \nlinks \nExplore Milford \nNews & Public Notices \nNews & Public Notices \nPosts \nlinks \nDiscover More News \nTown Reports \nTown Reports \nResources \ncontent \nTown Calendar              \r\n1 Union Square, Milford, NH 03055 \n6032490600  |  web@milford.nh.gov \nPowered By  Munibit  | © 2026 Terms  |  Privacy  |  Notifications  |  Accessibility Login                  \r\nSection Tools \r\n                         Manage Meeting Series \r\nHello  \r\nWhat is a Passkey? \n                Imagine signing into your account as easily as unlocking your phone—no more worrying about remembering or typing a password. A passkey is a secure digital key that uses the safety features in your device to keep your account protected. It’s designed to be both simple to use and highly secure. \n                Ready to experience a simpler, safer sign-in? Click the button above to create your passkey now. \r\nSign Up for Notifications! \r\n             Do not show again \r\nFill out the following fields. \n                     Activate notifications by clicking or tapping on the verification messages we send. Completing the verification process confirms your consent. Notification categories can be edited later from an email message footer. \r\n ",
